course: dictionary
lesson: 8427
title: Short forms and French words: sa
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: SA is a short form, called an abbreviation. It can stand for South Australia or South Africa. Look at the words around it to decide which one it means.
explain: On an address, «Adelaide, SA» tells you that Adelaide is in South Australia, a state of Australia.
explain: «Sa» is also a French word. In «sa mère», it means his or her mother, because «sa» goes before a feminine noun such as «mère» (mother).
explain: A small «sa» in the middle of an English word is usually just a piece of a longer word. Read the whole word first.
fact: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer word or name.
fact: «SA» can mean South Australia or South Africa.
fact: «Sa» is a French word meaning his or her, used before a feminine noun, as in «sa sœur» (his or her sister).
fact: After a company name, «S.A.» is like «Ltd» or «Inc.» in some countries.
fact: Check the language before you decide what a word means, because French words can look like English ones.
exercise: Which is the short form of South Australia? | Australia Ltd | Adelaide | Sah | *SA
exercise: «Sa mère» means his or her mother. What does «sa» mean here? | and | yes | the | *his or her
exercise: In «Adelaide, SA», what does SA tell you? | SA is a type of dog | *Adelaide is in South Australia | Adelaide is a company | Adelaide is a French word
test: Which French word fits here: «___ mère» (his or her mother)? | ses | mon | son | *sa
test: After a company name, what does «S.A.» mean in some countries? | A type of dog | A French word for sister | A town in Africa | *Like «Ltd» or «Inc.»
exam: Lily reads «sa sœur» in a French book and sees «SA» on a map. What is the best way to know which meaning is right? | Use the first meaning you find, always | *Read the words around it and check the language | Guess the one you like | Ignore both and skip the page
